  "limitations": [
    "Initial execution still uses the complete Supervisor. The split concerns cleanup recovery only.",
    "Fault cases use the existing Docker CLI simulator and real fakeworkload code; the separate success case uses an actual container.",
    "Most crash cases advance their disposable Run lease timestamp before recovery. The timer case waits for a live three-second lease to expire.",
    "Lost cleanup claim responses are modeled by discarding a committed return value; transport failure after claim commit was not injected.",
    "Both worker subprocess helper tests intentionally skip outside subprocess mode.",
    "Production operating cost, distributed-host/storage loss, version migration, network partitions, termination and provider workflows were not tested.",
    "The broader real-Docker/browser suites were not enabled. The prior full root suite had one umask-sensitive credential fixture failure; the unchanged package passed its umask-022 rerun."
  ],
